/-!
# Local generators of a strict transform

Let `F` be a finite type quasi-coherent module on an algebraic space `Bsp`, let `Z ⊆ Bsp` be the
closed subspace cut out by the `k`-th Fitting ideal sheaf of `F`, and let `b : Bsp' ⟶ Bsp` be the
blowup of `Bsp` in `Z`.  Then the strict transform of `F` — the quotient of its pullback to
`Bsp ×_{Bsp} Bsp'` by the sections supported on the inverse image of the exceptional divisor,
Stacks 0862 (1) — can locally be generated by `k` sections.

**The geometry.**  For `b` the blowup of `Bsp` in `Z`, the inverse image along the projection
`Bsp ×_{Bsp} Bsp' ⟶ Bsp'` of the exceptional divisor `b^{-1}Z` is an effective Cartier divisor
on `Bsp ×_{Bsp} Bsp'`, hence locally principal, and on affine charts it is cut out by a
nonzerodivisor.

**The Fitting ideal on a chart.**  Over the source chart of a diagram of affine étale charts, the
`k`-th Fitting ideal of the sections of the pullback of `F` is the defining ideal of the inverse
image of `Z`.

**The commutative algebra.**  Let `M` be a finite module over a commutative ring `R` whose `k`-th
Fitting ideal is generated by one element `f`.  Around every prime there is one element `h` of
`R`, not in that prime, and `k` elements of `M`, such that some power of `h` carries every
element of `M` into the submodule they span together with the `f`-power torsion
`Ideal.primaryComponent M (Ideal.span {f})`.  Stacks 0859 (2) identifies that torsion with the
supported sections on an affine chart.

**The sheaf theory.**  Given a sheaf submodule `K ⊆ M` of an `𝒪_X`-module and finitely many
sections of `M` over an étale chart `V` which, together with the sections of `K`, generate the
sections of `M` over every *affine* chart over `V`, the images of those sections in the cokernel
of `K` are generating sections of the restriction of the cokernel to `V`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.strictTransformSheaf_isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite`: the strict transform
  of `F` is locally generated by `k` sections.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_exceptionalPreimage_id`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.hasEffectiveCartierEtalePullbacks_exceptionalPreimage_id`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_openChart_isRegular_span_exceptionalPreimage_id` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocallyPrincipal_exceptionalPreimage_id`: the geometry, as an
  effective Cartier divisor, as condition (3) of Stacks 083C, in the chartwise form, and as local
  principality; `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocallyPrincipal_of_hasEffectiveCartierEtalePullbacks`
  is the general passage from condition (3) of Stacks 083C to Stacks 083B (1).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fittingIdealOnChart_modulePullback_eq_definingIdealAt`: the Fitting
  ideal on a chart.
* `Stacks.Fitting.exists_notMem_and_fin_span_sup_primaryComponent`: the commutative algebra
  after clearing denominators.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.preimage_chartPointsMap_range_ι_eq_zeroLocus` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_supportedSectionsSubmodule_iff_mem_primaryComponent`: the point
  set of a closed subspace on an affine chart is the zero locus of its defining ideal, and
  therefore Stacks 0859 (2) identifies the supported sections with the ideal-power torsion.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.generatesLocally_cokernel_π_of_le_span_sup` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.cokernelGeneratingSectionsOfLeSpanSup`: the sheaf theory, in the
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.GeneratesLocally` form and in the
  `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections` form.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.le_span_sup_of_isUnit_chartRestrict`: a chartwise generating family
  modulo a subsheaf, valid after inverting one function, generates over every affine chart above
  on which that function is invertible.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_chartDiagram_isRegular_span_definingIdealAt`: through every
  point of every chart there is an affine chart diagram on whose source chart the defining ideal
  is generated by a nonzerodivisor.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_cokernel_of_pointwise_span` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_cokernel_supportedSections_of_pointwise`:
  local generation of a cokernel from pointwise chart data.

